// case: arena-refusal-leaves-one-diagnostic
// what: `val arena = 7` is refused because every function this compiler emits
//      already takes an OrbitArena* arena, and the refusal returned without
//      declaring the name. The next read then reported `arena` undeclared and
//      counted a resolution miss, so the refusal contradicted itself. The
//      refusal now declares the name with the poisoned spelling, which the
//      checker accepts for every expected type and names as a type nowhere, so
//      the read stays silent. `one-diagnostic:` pins the count, and the
//      `expect-error:` line pins the wording.
// expect-error: Cannot declare 'arena'
// one-diagnostic:

fn main() -> int {
    val arena = 7
    return arena
}
